// nfct IS conntrack-tools' HELPER-OBJECT CLI, AND IS NOT THE `conntrack` BINARY. `conntrack` reads
// the flow and expectation tables; `nfct` manages the USERSPACE helper objects that create
// expectations. They are separate programs in the same upstream project, so they are separate
// authorities here rather than one module with two spellings.
data nfct_program: NonEmptyStr = "nfct"

// NO ArgvCommand BUILDER HERE, DELIBERATELY. The only consumer in this repository reaches this
// program through a privileged read projection that prepends its own sudo binary path, so it needs
// the ARGUMENT WORDS and not a command whose program field it would discard. Adding a builder
// nothing calls would be the dangling declaration DESIGN 3c refuses; it belongs here the day a
// direct invocation exists to consume it.
//
// `helper list` PRINTS THE REGISTERED USERSPACE HELPERS, one stanza per helper, and an empty stdout
// with exit zero is the honest empty reading. It is the counterpart to the kernel-side
// nf_conntrack_helper sysctl: a host can have automatic assignment gone from the kernel and still
// carry userspace helpers, so neither reading substitutes for the other.
data nfct_helper_list_arguments: List<NonEmptyStr> = ["helper", "list"]
